course: dictionary
lesson: 11354
title: One word, three zodiacs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Zodiac is one of these words. Read the clues around it: «The twelve zodiac animals go round in order, Rat, Ox, Tiger, Rabbit...» Animals going round in order tells you this zodiac is the Chinese one, a list of animals, not a list of stars.
explain: Now read this: «The zodiac is a band of twelve star patterns across the sky that the Sun and Moon seem to move through.» The clues are sky, stars and the Sun, so zodiac means star patterns in space. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with «star sign». In astrology, people believe their star sign, based on their birthday, controls their personality and luck. That is a belief, not science: studies have found no such effect. Horoscopes in magazines are for fun.
fact: The zodiac is a band of twelve star patterns, called constellations, across the sky.
fact: In astrology, the zodiac is split into twelve signs, such as Aries, Leo and Pisces.
fact: The Chinese zodiac is a cycle of twelve animals, one for each year, such as Rat, Ox, Tiger and Dragon.
fact: The same Chinese zodiac animal comes back every 12 years. The dragon is the only one of the twelve that is not a real animal.
fact: Astrology is not science. Studies have found no link between star signs and personality.
exercise: «The zodiac is a band of twelve star patterns across the sky.» What does zodiac mean here? | *A band of twelve star patterns in the sky | A fast kind of boat | A song sung at New Year | A sweet, sticky treat
exercise: «The twelve zodiac animals go round in order, so the same animal comes back every 12 years.» How often does the same Chinese zodiac animal come back? | Every 100 years | Every 5 years | Every year | *Every 12 years
exercise: Which zodiac animal is not a real animal? | Ox | Tiger | Rat | *Dragon
test: Your «star sign» depends on which part of your life? | Your height | Your favourite colour | *Your birthday | Your shoe size
test: Does science show that star signs control personality? | Yes, every scientist agrees | Only for people born in winter | Yes, but only on Mondays | *No, studies have found no such effect
exam: In «nǐ shǔ shénme?», what does the question ask? | How old are you? | *Which zodiac animal are you? | Where do you live? | What is your name?
